{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775334196-ZwT9eqoGTyfKnx3xnTnv","role":"assistant","created":1775334213,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I can extract the monthly sales data. Let me filter for the periods we need:\n\nJuly 1969–July 1970 (from August 1970 bulletin):\n- 1960-July: 389 (skip - this is July 1960)\n- Aug.: 348 (this is 1969 Aug based on context)\n- Sept.: 321\n- Oct.: 404\n- Nov.: 274\n- Dec.: 346\n- 1970-Jan.: 381\n- Feb.: 383\n- Mar.: 427\n- Apr.: 366\n- May: 367\n- June: 446\n- July: 393\n\nWait, I need to be more careful here. Looking at the table structure from the August bulletin:\n- It shows months from 1960-July, Aug., Sept., Oct., Nov., Dec., then 1970-Jan., Feb., Mar., Apr., May, June, July\n\nSince this is the August 1970 bulletin with cumulative data through July 31, 1970, the months listed after Dec. (1969) are:\n- 1970-Jan., Feb., Mar., Apr., May, June, July\n\nBut what about Aug., Sept., Oct., Nov., Dec. before 1970? Looking at the data:\n- 1960-July: 389 \n- Aug.: 348\n- Sept.: 321\n- Oct.: 404\n- Nov.: 274\n- Dec.: 346\n- 1970-Jan.: 381\n...\n\nGiven the context (this is from the August 1970 bulletin), the Aug., Sept., Oct., Nov., Dec. listed must be from 1969 (since 1970 months start with 1970-Jan).\n\nWait, let me re-examine. Looking at the text file again:\n```\n<tr><td>1960-July</td><td>389</td>\n\n\n<tr><td>Aug.</td><td>348</td>\n<tr><td>Sept.</td><td>321</td>\n<tr><td>Oct.</td><td>404</td>\n<tr><td>Nov.</td><td>274</td>\n<tr><td>Dec.</td><td>346</td>\n<tr><td>1970-Jan.</td><td>381</td>\n```\n\nSo for July 1969–July 1970, I need Aug. 1969 (348) through July 1970 (393). The August bulletin lists August through December 1969 followed by the first seven months of 1970, giving me the complete range I need.\n\nThe September bulletin extends this further to include August 1970 (388), so I have coverage from August 1969 through August 1970.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_ba13e370682e408baca94c98","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport re\n\n# Parse August 1970 bulletin to get monthly sales\n# Looking at the table, months are listed after the header 'Months:'\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1970_08_page_70.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content_08 = f.read()\n\n# Find the months section - need to look for specific pattern\n# The months section in August bulletin has Aug., Sept., Oct., Nov., Dec. (1969) then 1970-Jan. to July\n# Using a more specific pattern\n\n# Find the SB-2 table section (Sales and Redemptions by Periods, All Series Combined)\n# The months data follows 'Months:' and ends before '</table>'\nmonths_pattern = r'<tr><td>(Months:)</td>.*?</table>'\nmatch = re.search(months_pattern, content_08, re.DOTALL)\nif match:\n    months_section = match.group(0)\n    print('August bulletin months section:')\n    # Now extract individual month rows\n    rows = re.findall(r'<tr><td>([^<]+)</td><td>([0-9,]+)</td>', months_section)\n    for period, sales in rows:\n        if period != 'Months:':\n            print(f'{period}: {sales}')\n\nprint()\nprint('---')\n\n# Same for September 1970 bulletin\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1970_09_page_70.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content_09 = f.read()\n\nmatch = re.search(months_pattern, content_09, re.DOTALL)\nif match:\n    months_section = match.group(0)\n    print('September bulletin months section:')\n    rows = re.findall(r'<tr><td>([^<]+)</td><td>([0-9,]+)</td>', months_section)\n    for period, sales in rows:\n        if period != 'Months:':\n            print(f'{period}: {sales}')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
